▪️Ansarallah's advances in Yemen appear to be a positive development for Iran and its network alliances - however the organization has previously held this territory, it extends (perhaps overextends) the organization in terms of operations and logistics, and may feed into US objectives rather than oppose them; 

▪️The US is waging war on Iran to disrupt energy exports from all of West Asia - closing additional maritime transit points only enhances US energy dominance strategies; 

▪️Hezbollah is currently facing setbacks as Israeli forces encroach further into Lebanon - enabled by the US-backed 2024 collapse of Syria; 

▪️All of these conflicts are being fought to diminish Iran's network alliances in addition to Iran itself; 

▪️Tech CEO Eric Schmidt admits that Ukraine is losing the innovation race against Russia but appears oblivious to the fundamental factors causing this deficiency; 

▪️US ambitions toward the Moon may include a desire to hold the "high ground" at the top of Earth's gravity well and to disrupt Chinese plans to develop an Earth-Moon economic zone;
